===Etymology===
{{etyl|gd|en}} {{compound|gd|Mac|Kenzie|t1=son of|t2=the intelligent one" or possibly "the wise ruler|nocat=1}} or “the bright one/the one born of fire”. Possible alternate: Gaelic {{m|und|MacCoinneach||Son of Kenneth}}. Originally a surname, the family motto being “I shine, not burn.”

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}
{{slim-wikipedia}}
{{wikipedia|Mackenzie River}}

# {{surname|from=Scottish Gaelic|dot=}} of [[Scottish]] origin.
# {{given name|female|from=surnames}}, transferred use of the surname since the 1970s, also in the form [[Makenzie]].
# {{given name|male}}
# A river in the [[Northwest Territories]], the longest in [[Canada]], running from [[Great Slave Lake]] to the [[Beaufort Sea]].

